Package: libsixsv2
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: 6SV2.1 atmospheric correction library
 A C11 port of the 6SV2.1 (Second Simulation of the Satellite Signal in
 the Solar Spectrum) radiative transfer model for operational atmospheric
 correction of multispectral and hyperspectral remote sensing imagery.
 .
 It provides scalar and polarized DISCOM radiative transfer, satellite and
 aircraft paths, standard and BDM aerosol models, and an AOD by water-vapour by
 wavelength LUT. Operational C extensions include Lambertian and BRDF-coupled
 inversion, retrieval, terrain, adjacency, uncertainty and spatial routines.
 Selected LUT and image loops use OpenMP.

Package: libsixsv-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends: libsixsv2 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: 6SV2.1 atmospheric correction library - development files
 Development headers, pkg-config metadata and linker symlink for the libsixsv
 SONAME 2 C ABI.
 .
 Install this package to build C or C++ programs that call libsixsv. The package
 installs all headers under /usr/include/sixsv/; there is no Python wrapper
 package, although the C ABI can be loaded directly with ctypes.
